@@ -360,6 +360,46 @@ User --> Claude Code / CLI
 
 ---
 
+## OpenAI-compatible connections
+
+`providers test -p openai` and MCP `agent_execute` share the saved OpenAI
+connection settings. For a local compatible server:
+
+```bash
+ruflo providers configure -p openai -e http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1 -m local-model
+ruflo providers test -p openai
+ruflo agent spawn --provider openai --model local-model
+```
+
+Call MCP `agent_execute` with the returned agent ID. Both a base root and a
+terminal `/v1` are accepted, including gateway prefixes such as `/api/v1`.
+Custom endpoints require a configured or explicitly selected execution model;
+the probe can run before choosing a model. Canonical OpenAI uses `gpt-4o` when
+no model was selected. An explicit agent model wins over the saved model;
+automatically routed Claude/vendor model IDs are not forwarded to OpenAI.
+
+A custom endpoint saved in project config receives only the key saved beside
+it, or no Authorization header for an anonymous server. It never receives the
+ambient `OPENAI_API_KEY`. An explicit `OPENAI_BASE_URL` uses `OPENAI_API_KEY`;
+a saved key is a fallback only when its normalized endpoint matches that URL.
+Without a custom URL, the canonical endpoint requires a saved or environment
+key. Invalid URLs, configuration load errors and malformed settings fail before
+network access. Query strings, fragments and URL userinfo are not supported.
+
+An explicit agent provider takes precedence over `RUFLO_PROVIDER`. Existing
+Anthropic, OpenRouter and Ollama inference retains priority. When none applies,
+OpenAI settings (including `OPENAI_API_KEY` alone) can now select OpenAI for
+execution, even if that key was previously used only for embeddings. OpenAI
+failures do not enter the cross-provider fallback chain. Existing Ollama
+fallback and Claude-tier learning/health bookkeeping are unchanged.
+
+Provider commands use the current working directory. MCP execution keeps its
+existing `CLAUDE_FLOW_CWD` override, except for filesystem roots or HOME. The
+connection helper does not change either path. The default official request
+uses `max_completion_tokens`; custom servers use `max_tokens`. Temperature is
+sent only when explicitly supplied. No real OpenAI service is exercised by the
+loopback regression tests.
+
 ## Documentation
 
 Four docs for four audiences:
